      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Happy to see the PNG decoding move to Rust, too. Does any of this need to be runtime-switchable or are we strictly making the decoder choice at compile time?\n\nSo far making a compile-time choice seemed sufficient. \n\n\u003e \u003e I am not quite happy with having an ad-hoc helper for Rust-vs-libpng dispatching inside Fontations-related code (rather than in src/codec/...). But this seems okay for now, as a first step\n\u003e \n\u003e Yes, this is also something I found surprising/in an unusual place in the `SkTypeface_fontations.cpp`. As a compromise, could we have it in a separate header in `ports/`, would that make it easier? What\u0027s the obstacle in putting it into src/codec?\n\nI initially thought that we\u0027d have to introduce yet another target (introduce new Blaze target + introduce new/separate gni list + adopt the new new gni list in Chromium and in Flutter).  But after thinking about it now, I may see a way to reuse the existing targets:\n\n* Add new header (declaring impl-agnostic API for decoding a PNG) to *both* `skia_codec_libpng_srcs` and ``.\n* Add a `libpng`-based-impl in `third_party/skia/src/codec/SkPngCodec.cpp` and \na Rust-based-impl in `third_party/skia/experimental/rust_png/decoder/impl/SkPngRustCodec.cpp`.\n* The above (compared to implementing in a single source file) has some risk of having two conflicting definitions/implementations.  But we can enforce in the header that exactly one decoder impl is active (i.e. `#error`-out if two are active or zero are active).\n\n\u003e That said, I don\u0027t see this as a blocker, but I\u0027d let Florin or Ben decide on that. With that, LGTM from my side, but let\u0027s hear it from Skia folks.\n\nAck.  The idea I have spelled above seems ok, so let me try implementing that (i.e. keeping only myself in the attention set for now + unresolving this comment).",
