      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is there a precedent or an obvious path forward for this?  Otherwise I probably should create a small design note to help us discuss how to do that.  My initial idea would be to:\n\n*  Top-level `//BUILD.bazel`:\n    * Use https://bazel.build/extending/config#defining-build-settings to define a new flag\n    * Let\u0027s make it a **string** flag + assert that it is either 1) not set / empty, 2) \"libpng\", or 3) \"Rust PNG\".  (Alternative: 2 boolean flags + assert that both are not enabled at the same time.  Maybe this more closely mimics the GN world and therefore may be desirable?)\n* `//src/codec`:   \n    * Introduce an `alias` in `//src/codec/BUILD.bazel` that `select`-s either `//src/codec:png_decode` or `//experimental/rust_png/decoder` based on the flag.\n* `//src/codec:png_decode` or `//experimental/rust_png/decoder`\n    * Transitively depending on the actual decoder impls should set a `#define` like `SK_CODEC_DECODES_PNG_WITH_LIBPNG`.  In the GN world I would do this by exposing a `public_configs`, but I don\u0027t know how to do that in Bazel...",
